    "procurement": "Purchase IT equipment, furniture, and supplies for the bank. Issue Requests for Proposals (RFPs) and tender calls. Negotiate pricing, terms, and SLAs with vendors. Generate and authorize Purchase Orders (POs). Draft and finalize formal contracts with suppliers. Verify that delivered goods meet quality and quantity standards. Conduct annual performance evaluations of critical vendors. Control the procurement budget and identify cost savings. Maintain optimal inventory levels at the central warehouse. Ensure a transparent and corruption-free bidding process. Onboard new vendors and conduct due diligence. Manage software license renewals and vendor subscriptions. Resolve disputes regarding defective products or delayed deliveries. Coordinate with Accounts Payable for timely vendor payments. Maintain the approved vendor list. Ensure vendors comply with the bank's ESG and ethical standards. Standardize office equipment across all bank branches. Manage the procurement of secure printing (cheques, cards). Review logistics and distribution costs for branch supplies. Track and report procurement metrics to management.",
